---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Writing" description="Essays on identity, security, AI agents, and building things in the open.">
<style>
  .head { padding: 56px 0 8px; max-width: 46rem; }
  .head p { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 8px; }
  .head a { color: var(--amber); }
  .head a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .list { max-width: 46rem; margin-top: 28px; }
  .note { margin-top: 24px; font-size: .88rem; color: var(--text-3); }
  .note a { color: var(--teal); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/writing" />

<main class="wrapb">
  <div class="head">
    <h1 class="statement">Writing</h1>
    <p>Mostly identity, and increasingly the identity of AI agents. New here? The agentic series is the spine: <a href="/writing/ai-agents-identity">the problem</a>, <a href="/writing/agent-identity-gap">the gap</a>, <a href="/writing/the-workload-is-the-reasoning-session">the argument</a>, and <a href="/writing/the-credential-remembers-who">the mechanism</a> — with <a href="/model">the framework</a> tying it together.</p>
  </div>

